  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\ge 36$ using the absolute value method.",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 36 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{36} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\nx\\le -6\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-6]\\cup [6,\\infty ).$",
